WEBVTT

00:02.170 --> 00:04.870
<i>The students are exhausted, too.</i>

00:04.870 --> 00:08.200
Some mutants appeared among 
the students, after all.

00:08.200 --> 00:10.010
It caused quite the commotion.

00:10.010 --> 00:15.120
They've been regarding each other with 
caution and can't return to their own rooms.

00:15.120 --> 00:17.240
They couldn't be more anxious.

00:17.240 --> 00:21.640
That all ends today. Are you two ready?

00:23.070 --> 00:24.380
Time to act.

00:42.140 --> 00:44.020
<b>Season Two</b>

01:55.090 --> 01:59.550
<b>Night Nineteen    The Unruly Merchant</b>

01:55.090 --> 01:59.550
<b>Night Nineteen    The Unruly Merchant</b>

01:59.510 --> 02:01.460
<i>You're looking better than I expected.</i>

02:01.460 --> 02:02.310
Sir!

02:02.800 --> 02:04.230
<i>How are you feeling?</i>

02:04.230 --> 02:05.510
We're fine.

02:05.510 --> 02:07.050
What's the situation in the city?

02:07.480 --> 02:09.030
<i>Not good.</i>

02:09.030 --> 02:10.950
<i>The number of mutants hasn't gone down,</i>

02:10.950 --> 02:13.010
<i>and support from other nations 
hasn't arrived yet.</i>

02:16.540 --> 02:19.480
Sir, let us help exterminate the mutants.

02:19.480 --> 02:21.120
We can fight them, too.

02:21.410 --> 02:23.620
<i>Calm down. That would be suicide.</i>

02:23.620 --> 02:24.490
But...

02:24.490 --> 02:26.650
We just want to help.

02:26.650 --> 02:28.840
We fought Ilumgand, didn't we?

02:29.240 --> 02:31.390
<i>The headmaster has ordered me to go</i>

02:31.390 --> 02:34.330
<i>to the northeastern section where 
the merchant's guild is located.</i>

02:35.060 --> 02:38.020
<i>What if this place is 
attacked while I'm gone?</i>

02:39.210 --> 02:44.650
<i>If more students mutate, 
everyone in the dorms will be killed.</i>

02:44.650 --> 02:45.850
<i>Do you still want to go?</i>

02:49.390 --> 02:50.660
We'll stay.

02:50.940 --> 02:51.560
<i>Hm?</i>

02:51.560 --> 02:52.930
We'll stay here.

02:52.930 --> 02:55.250
We'll work together to defend this place.

02:55.250 --> 02:56.400
For Shiki-san, too.

02:56.770 --> 02:59.370
<i>I'm encouraged to hear that. 
I'm counting on you.</i>

02:59.370 --> 03:00.300
Let's do this.

03:00.300 --> 03:01.020
Yeah.

03:01.020 --> 03:02.570
We'll protect the dorms.

03:02.570 --> 03:03.310
Yeah.

03:03.570 --> 03:06.280
Aqua and Eris, look after them.

03:06.280 --> 03:08.490
Aw, man. We gotta babysit the newbies?

03:08.490 --> 03:09.280
Hey!

03:33.430 --> 03:36.190
Those are the two the 
young master summoned.

03:36.460 --> 03:38.920
Rembrandt must be here, too.

03:38.920 --> 03:42.610
Mio, don't do anything to 
the guild representative.

03:42.610 --> 03:44.270
I wouldn't dream of it.

03:44.270 --> 03:47.130
Even if he's been attacked by monsters, 
I won't do anything at all.

03:47.130 --> 03:49.320
Y-You should help him if he's being attacked.

03:50.360 --> 03:51.230
Very well.

03:51.230 --> 03:52.910
<i>Why did she look away?</i>

03:55.750 --> 03:57.430
Kuzunoha-dono!

03:58.190 --> 04:00.120
Are my daughters all right?

04:00.450 --> 04:02.720
They haven't joined the fighting, have they?

04:03.010 --> 04:06.560
<i>Don't worry. I assigned some dependable 
people to secretly watch over them.</i>

04:07.150 --> 04:08.970
Good.

04:08.970 --> 04:11.360
We meet again, Kuzunoha.

04:12.950 --> 04:15.760
<i>I feel slightly dizzy and nauseous.</i>

04:15.760 --> 04:18.570
<i>He's definitely my least favorite 
person after the goddess.</i>

04:19.540 --> 04:22.240
I heard you'd be joining 
the extermination squads.

04:22.240 --> 04:23.950
Was your shop all right?

04:24.270 --> 04:26.630
<i>No, it was destroyed.</i>

04:26.630 --> 04:29.410
<i>There was no damage to my employees 
or merchandise, though.</i>

04:29.690 --> 04:32.790
I see. I'm glad they're all right.

04:32.790 --> 04:35.160
<i>What? Glad they're all right?</i>

04:36.970 --> 04:39.450
He seems rather different from 
last time, doesn't he?

04:39.450 --> 04:45.020
Not even he can act so feisty after you 
loaned us such dependable guards.

04:45.020 --> 04:45.960
Right?

04:46.370 --> 04:47.630
Silence!

04:47.630 --> 04:51.170
But to think you employed 
such monstrous servants...

04:51.170 --> 04:54.960
I revealed your circumstances only to him.

04:54.960 --> 04:58.280
I figured it would make 
things go more smoothly.

04:58.700 --> 05:01.750
<i>I saw signs of looting on my way here.</i>

05:01.750 --> 05:05.470
<i>What's the extent of the damage 
the merchant's guild is aware of?</i>

05:06.110 --> 05:07.730
We don't know the specifics.

05:07.730 --> 05:10.440
Without adequate forces, 
there's nothing we can do.

05:10.440 --> 05:13.610
He's a real pain in the rear, isn't he?

05:13.610 --> 05:16.590
I keep telling him we'll be 
fine as long as you're—

05:15.820 --> 05:17.660
Pat, enough already!

05:18.480 --> 05:19.670
<i>Pat?</i>

05:20.050 --> 05:23.540
<i>Oh, because his name is Patrick?</i>

05:24.520 --> 05:28.400
Anyway, this is how the 
merchant's guild is holding up.

05:28.400 --> 05:30.350
He's handling it better than most, too.

05:30.860 --> 05:33.790
More than a few guild members 
have suffered such massive losses

05:33.790 --> 05:36.090
that they've lost their minds.

05:36.690 --> 05:39.450
It's not a pretty sight.

05:40.130 --> 05:44.950
<i>We'll take over exterminating 
mutants in this area.</i>

05:44.950 --> 05:50.410
<i>If you can get in touch with them, you can 
have your personal forces return here.</i>

05:50.900 --> 05:54.880
So this isn't even a threat to you.

05:54.880 --> 05:57.410
<i>We took care of about fifteen on our way here.</i>

05:57.410 --> 05:58.480
What?

05:58.480 --> 06:00.380
<i>Also, in this area...</i>

06:00.380 --> 06:02.560
Nine mutants remain.

06:02.560 --> 06:05.120
No new mutants have appeared.

06:05.880 --> 06:11.010
<i>The academy has identified the 
accessories causing the mutations,</i>

06:11.010 --> 06:13.350
<i>so I ask that you assist 
with retrieving those.</i>

06:13.350 --> 06:16.230
<i>She'll fill you in on the specifics.</i>

06:16.230 --> 06:17.570
Who, me?

06:20.250 --> 06:22.440
You have our full cooperation.

06:22.440 --> 06:25.530
<i>He's like a completely different person.</i>

06:27.570 --> 06:30.390
Nine mutants remaining, right?

06:30.390 --> 06:34.400
Yes, including those currently 
engaged in combat.

06:34.400 --> 06:39.580
Once we take care of those, 
let's make it a contest between you two.

06:39.580 --> 06:40.920
Your prize will be...

06:42.070 --> 06:45.680
How about if I fulfill one 
request from the winner?

06:45.680 --> 06:46.920
What?!

06:46.920 --> 06:48.920
A-Are you sure about that?

06:48.920 --> 06:50.800
No taking it back later.

06:51.080 --> 06:54.810
Yeah. Try to limit your request to 
something I can actually fulfill.

06:55.390 --> 06:58.490
I wouldn't dream of doing 
anything so ignoble.

06:58.490 --> 07:00.530
Young Master, prepare yourself.

07:01.820 --> 07:03.980
Who is that man?

07:03.980 --> 07:06.370
Zara, you're sweating bullets.

07:06.860 --> 07:11.340
More than fifty mercenaries defeated 
four mutants in three days.

07:11.340 --> 07:14.440
Yet he claims to have beaten fifteen?

07:14.880 --> 07:17.670
But he's just a boy who 
was frightened by me.

07:18.370 --> 07:22.790
It was time you learned your lesson.

07:22.790 --> 07:26.000
Who is Kuzunoha actually?

07:26.000 --> 07:29.710
As you know, he's a naïve 
and inexperienced merchant.

07:29.710 --> 07:32.570
Pat, cut the crap.

07:33.390 --> 07:35.940
He seemed that way because you 
only looked at the surface.

07:35.940 --> 07:40.670
I was hoping you'd see past 
that. You disappoint me.

07:40.670 --> 07:44.940
He's so naïve, he doesn't know the 
first thing about being a merchant.

07:45.510 --> 07:47.620
How to talk to other merchants,

07:47.620 --> 07:49.790
laying the groundwork for future endeavors,

07:49.790 --> 07:52.410
establishing prices based on the market...

07:52.410 --> 07:55.130
He understands less than half of that.

07:55.130 --> 07:56.870
"Sell quality goods as cheaply as possible."

07:56.870 --> 08:00.280
That's truly all he has on his mind.

08:00.280 --> 08:04.090
Selling quality goods as cheaply 
as possible is the basis of trade.

08:04.530 --> 08:08.240
Didn't we say the same thing 
when we became merchants?

08:08.240 --> 08:12.100
Yes, but such naïveté won't get you far.

08:12.720 --> 08:18.300
Breaking into vested interests requires 
utilizing and killing people with money.

08:18.600 --> 08:23.270
Trade isn't about ideals. 
It is firmly rooted in reality.

08:23.270 --> 08:28.480
You're right, but after 
learning of their strength,

08:28.480 --> 08:31.500
how many merchants could 
negotiate honestly with them?

08:31.500 --> 08:33.870
Are you saying we should use violence 
to bend trade to our desires?

08:34.580 --> 08:40.050
We can't, Pat. The goddess would punish 
us swiftly for such selfish behavior.

08:40.050 --> 08:43.070
Are you sure her punishment would reach us?

08:43.390 --> 08:45.730
I bet on it not reaching us.

08:45.730 --> 08:50.160
So no matter what anyone says, I won't stop 
supporting the Kuzunoha Trading Company.

08:50.520 --> 08:53.850
You think their insolence 
will go unpunished?

08:53.850 --> 08:59.060
A man needs to be insolent 
to make his ideals reality.

09:00.190 --> 09:03.000
He's reaching beyond trade 
to create an organization

09:03.000 --> 09:05.600
that removes illness and 
curses from the world.

09:05.600 --> 09:09.060
Getting involved in such a great 
undertaking isn't so bad.

09:09.060 --> 09:12.060
To put it in a way that makes me 
sound like the man you know,

09:12.060 --> 09:15.820
"It's worth betraying anything 
to seize this golden egg."

09:16.220 --> 09:20.080
Even hyumankind—no, the goddess herself?

09:20.370 --> 09:23.680
If money is everything 
and profits make right,

09:23.680 --> 09:26.960
then isn't betrayal part of business, too?

09:26.960 --> 09:28.700
But what you're proposing is...

09:29.650 --> 09:34.290
I know. If that's what you really think, 
then make money off of the war.

09:34.750 --> 09:40.200
But neither you nor I have 
profited off of war.

09:40.980 --> 09:45.770
I lost my entire family to war.

09:45.770 --> 09:48.770
I lost my brother and his wife.

09:48.770 --> 09:54.160
Since then, you and I have traded like mad, 
relying only on ourselves and money.

09:54.160 --> 09:59.030
I know. That's why Kuzunoha 
irritates me so much.

09:59.880 --> 10:04.490
You should visit Tsige sometime. 
It'll change your thinking.

10:04.490 --> 10:07.110
I'll have my daughters show you around.

10:07.660 --> 10:10.840
You mean Shifu-chan? 
She's grown quite beautiful.

10:10.840 --> 10:14.050
What? I didn't say anything about Shifu.

10:14.290 --> 10:18.270
Did you think I meant Shifu, 
who looks just like your old flame Lisa?

10:18.270 --> 10:20.180
N-No, I...

10:20.180 --> 10:24.530
We're the best of friends. 
I trust you completely.

10:25.050 --> 10:29.780
Did you really think I'd say that? Get over her!

10:28.220 --> 10:31.200
Don't, Pat! Stop!

10:32.570 --> 10:35.980
We'll hit the northwestern section next. 
That's the craftsmen's neighborhood, right?

10:35.980 --> 10:40.780
Yes. The academy is taking care of 
the more affluent neighborhoods.

10:40.780 --> 10:41.910
They couldn't be more obvious.

10:41.910 --> 10:45.370
Young Master, I've finished 
collecting accessories.

10:45.370 --> 10:49.790
I provided the guild representative 
with food, water, and blankets.

10:49.790 --> 10:53.590
I told him to mention the Kuzunoha Trading 
Company's name when he distributed them.

10:53.590 --> 10:54.940
Good work.

10:54.940 --> 10:57.340
I'm surprised Zara-san 
accepted those conditions.

10:57.920 --> 11:00.550
He gets to save the townsfolk for free.

11:00.550 --> 11:03.070
Even if he weren't a merchant, 
he'd accept our terms.

11:03.070 --> 11:06.440
By the way, Mio is in an oddly good mood.

11:06.440 --> 11:09.750
I'm having Mio and Shiki 
play a bit of a game.

11:09.750 --> 11:12.530
They're competing to see 
who can defeat more mutants.

11:13.250 --> 11:14.350
Take this.

11:14.350 --> 11:16.830
I see. Judging by her behavior...

11:16.830 --> 11:19.870
Yup. Mio is winning 4-2.

11:19.870 --> 11:22.840
I've agreed to fulfill one 
request from the winner.

11:22.840 --> 11:23.710
What?!

11:23.960 --> 11:26.730
What kind of unbelievably 
extravagant prize is that?!

11:26.730 --> 11:28.210
That's the first I've heard about it!

11:28.480 --> 11:31.510
Because I asked you to handle the guild.

11:31.510 --> 11:33.080
Now, time for work.

11:33.370 --> 11:35.610
Wait! I demand an explanation I can accept!

11:35.610 --> 11:38.620
I may have understood that, 
but I can't accept it!

11:38.620 --> 11:40.850
In other words, I insist that 
you hear my request, as well!

11:40.850 --> 11:42.560
Young Master!

11:42.560 --> 11:45.420
<i>For now, I'll head toward 
the northwestern section.</i>

11:45.420 --> 11:49.890
<i>Wait, I've already called in 
help over there, though...</i>

11:53.060 --> 11:55.080
Come at me.

11:55.670 --> 11:58.600
The great Mondo will take you on.

12:08.490 --> 12:10.570
Behold the forest ogres' 
ultimate technique.

12:10.570 --> 12:12.340
Death by tree!

12:14.700 --> 12:17.790
My tree-planting campaign's 
coming along nicely.

12:18.300 --> 12:19.010
Mondo.

12:19.380 --> 12:22.420
The bosses are on their way here.

12:22.710 --> 12:23.500
Oh, yeah?

12:23.990 --> 12:26.290
I'm sure my unworthy students 
have been causing trouble for them.

12:26.290 --> 12:28.580
It pains me to have to meet them.

12:28.580 --> 12:30.630
By "students," do you mean Aqua and Eris?

12:31.200 --> 12:33.520
The boss doesn't care about that.

12:33.520 --> 12:36.350
I'm relieved to hear that.

12:36.350 --> 12:40.650
The least I can do is live up to 
the young master's expectations.

12:42.670 --> 12:46.410
What's the aim of the ones who 
unleashed these creatures?

12:46.410 --> 12:49.390
Don't they know the young 
master would quash them?

12:49.390 --> 12:52.860
Beats me. I certainly don't 
know how demons think.

12:53.400 --> 12:56.700
All we have to do is whatever 
the boss needs us to do.

12:56.700 --> 13:00.950
You're right. By fighting like this...

13:02.800 --> 13:04.160
We make ourselves useful!

13:04.160 --> 13:05.220
Yeah!

13:09.110 --> 13:10.350
You lot!

13:10.350 --> 13:12.130
What are you doing?

13:12.130 --> 13:13.350
What do you mean?

13:13.350 --> 13:15.280
The same thing everyone else is doing.

13:15.280 --> 13:17.960
If you're still mobile, go assist 
the extermination forces!

13:17.960 --> 13:20.060
You call yourselves academy students?!

13:22.090 --> 13:23.900
What is it, Eris?

13:23.900 --> 13:27.040
The headmaster has lost his mind. 
He's trying to use the newbies.

13:27.400 --> 13:30.770
What should we do? The young 
master told us to protect them.

13:32.060 --> 13:33.990
I've got a nice idea.

13:33.990 --> 13:37.880
We'll use our killer technique 
to protect the entire dormitory.

13:38.270 --> 13:40.240
K-Killer technique?

13:41.530 --> 13:43.950
No way! Absolutely not!

13:43.950 --> 13:46.340
Fine. Then I'll do it myself.

13:46.340 --> 13:49.020
What? Can you cast that yourself?

13:49.020 --> 13:52.340
Of course. There's also a solo version. 
I need to borrow your mana, though.

13:52.340 --> 13:54.710
Come on, give it to me.

13:55.400 --> 13:56.950
Then hurry up and—

13:56.950 --> 13:57.600
You fell for it.

13:58.320 --> 13:59.890
M-My body...

14:00.620 --> 14:03.240
Now let's hold hands.

14:03.240 --> 14:06.040
No! Stop! Let go!

14:06.540 --> 14:10.620
Glitter, diamond of the heart!

14:06.540 --> 14:11.740
Move, body! Please! Move, move!

14:10.620 --> 14:12.300
Killer technique: Cocyt—

14:14.760 --> 14:17.330
Enough! I'll complete the spell!

14:17.570 --> 14:20.200
Killer technique: Cocyt—no, wait!

14:20.200 --> 14:22.790
Take this! Floral Tribute Ice Prison!

14:28.120 --> 14:29.420
Hey, Eris.

14:29.420 --> 14:31.360
Don't talk to me.

14:31.730 --> 14:34.320
How are we gonna get out?

14:38.770 --> 14:40.550
I'm sorry!

14:40.820 --> 14:44.080
I'll make sure those idiots 
are punished harshly!

14:44.080 --> 14:46.400
It's not your fault, Mondo.

14:46.700 --> 14:50.060
Shiki, they've got food in the dorms, right?

14:50.060 --> 14:53.470
Yes. They should be fine for several days.

14:53.470 --> 14:54.920
You heard him.

14:55.230 --> 14:57.090
Come on, raise your head.

14:57.090 --> 15:00.520
I appreciate your magnanimous words!

15:02.240 --> 15:04.380
Anyway, what should we do?

15:04.380 --> 15:06.350
Break it? Leave it alone?

15:06.350 --> 15:08.710
Wouldn't it be fine to leave it the way it is?

15:08.710 --> 15:11.420
It's needlessly hard. 
Breaking it would be a pain.

15:11.420 --> 15:13.220
It doesn't taste very good, either.

15:13.670 --> 15:17.110
I agree. Depending on the 
situation at the academy,

15:17.110 --> 15:19.600
they may attempt to send students to battle.

15:19.600 --> 15:25.220
You're right. I'll ask Aqua 
and Eris what happened later.

15:25.220 --> 15:29.610
Tomorrow, we'll liberate the remaining 
sections and continue distributing supplies.

15:29.610 --> 15:33.830
We don't know which nation will 
send supplies and troops first,

15:33.830 --> 15:36.900
but once they take over, 
our job will be done.

15:37.400 --> 15:42.510
Then the hyumans of the city will realize 
they're at war with the demons.

15:42.510 --> 15:45.550
What? You're going to expose the demons?

15:45.550 --> 15:47.970
No, the academy will discover the truth.

15:47.970 --> 15:51.430
I did a little something to the 
accessories we collected.

15:51.710 --> 15:54.390
They should notice within a couple of days,

15:54.390 --> 15:56.630
even if the people examining them are idiots.

15:56.630 --> 16:00.350
But isn't it bad for us if they 
find out demons are behind this?

16:00.890 --> 16:04.480
The Kuzunoha Trading Company is 
suspected of associating with demons.

16:04.480 --> 16:08.100
Nobody would believe that anymore.

16:08.100 --> 16:11.390
After all, we're heroes who 
did everything in our power

16:11.390 --> 16:14.580
to evacuate citizens and 
exterminate many mutants.

16:14.580 --> 16:16.060
<i>I see.</i>

16:16.520 --> 16:19.340
<i>These three truly are dependable.</i>

16:21.450 --> 16:24.670
So, why did you two cast this spell?

16:24.670 --> 16:26.160
W-Well, because...

16:26.160 --> 16:28.320
You went along with Eris's crazy plan?

16:28.320 --> 16:29.600
Something like that.

16:29.600 --> 16:30.130
Yup.

16:30.390 --> 16:35.920
But Young Master, I've been wondering, 
how did you get inside the barrier?

16:35.920 --> 16:37.930
Eris knows.

16:38.250 --> 16:40.390
Like a mole.

16:40.850 --> 16:43.220
So, anything else to report?

16:43.220 --> 16:44.960
Nothing in particular.

16:44.960 --> 16:46.420
No, there is something.

16:46.420 --> 16:46.970
What?

16:47.420 --> 16:51.950
There's probably some kind of mastermind 
where all the luxurious houses are.

16:51.950 --> 16:53.460
A mastermind?

16:54.050 --> 16:58.020
They're using some kind of special 
equipment to attract mutants there.

16:58.300 --> 17:00.860
Must be tough being rich.

17:00.860 --> 17:05.850
<i>That's an affluent area. 
The academy is focusing its efforts there.</i>

17:06.180 --> 17:08.590
Thanks, Eris. I appreciate it.

17:08.590 --> 17:13.000
You're too kind. Please forgive Aqua 
for casting her barrier, as well.

17:13.000 --> 17:13.790
What?!

17:13.790 --> 17:17.820
I'm not mad. Do you two want to leave?

17:17.820 --> 17:19.090
I'll take you with me.

17:19.090 --> 17:20.960
I-I'm fine for now.

17:20.960 --> 17:23.090
I've got a bad feeling about outside...

17:23.360 --> 17:24.690
<i>Two forest ogres,</i>

17:24.690 --> 17:26.090
<i>young enough to fear the wrath</i>

17:26.090 --> 17:27.390
<i>of their mad teacher.</i>

17:30.030 --> 17:31.240
Kuzunoha-dono.

17:33.220 --> 17:34.900
Did you just return?

17:35.180 --> 17:38.620
Kuzunoha-dono—rather, Kuzunoha-sama.

17:38.940 --> 17:43.830
I've come to understand a fraction of 
your power through this disturbance.

17:43.830 --> 17:47.710
<i>Oh, right. The important people in the 
city know what we've been up to.</i>

17:47.710 --> 17:52.580
Limia, Gritonia, and Laurel 
have a request for you.

17:53.510 --> 17:56.160
We'd like you to restore our 
telepathy as soon as possible.

17:56.730 --> 18:00.380
Naturally, we swear not to mention the 
Kuzunoha Trading Company's name.

18:00.720 --> 18:02.650
<i>Restoration of telepathy, huh?</i>

18:02.650 --> 18:05.230
<i>If I wanted to, I could do 
that right away, but...</i>

18:06.530 --> 18:09.690
This is the ability of the demihumans 
known as forest ogres, right?

18:10.000 --> 18:12.660
What an incredible barrier.

18:12.660 --> 18:17.700
How delightful that we're capable of 
surprising even the great Banshoku-dono.

18:17.990 --> 18:22.380
So, will the Kuzunoha Trading Company 
cease its activity tomorrow?

18:22.380 --> 18:26.750
That's the plan. Then we'll just be left 
with some troublesome cleanup to do.

18:26.750 --> 18:28.340
Troublesome, huh?

18:28.340 --> 18:30.630
Have you told Makoto-kun about that?

18:30.630 --> 18:34.910
If we told him now, things could end poorly.

18:34.910 --> 18:37.440
We've decided to handle 
it ourselves this time.

18:37.440 --> 18:38.550
I see.

18:38.550 --> 18:40.770
It's troublesome indeed.

18:40.770 --> 18:45.630
We were surprised to learn there was someone 
other than demons sneaking around.

18:46.210 --> 18:49.180
The demons had a collaborator 
other than the blue-skinned one.

18:49.180 --> 18:51.860
Mio will deal with them tonight.

18:51.860 --> 18:53.470
So scary.

18:53.470 --> 18:56.550
You're not going to let them explain 
themselves or protect them?

18:56.550 --> 19:01.240
I doubt we could use a demihuman 
who hates hyumans so much.

19:01.240 --> 19:03.920
Besides... One moment.

19:05.190 --> 19:08.670
Yes, that's fine. I'll leave the method up to you.

19:08.670 --> 19:10.970
We'll speak again later.

19:10.970 --> 19:13.000
A telepathic message? From whom?

19:13.270 --> 19:14.390
The young master.

19:14.390 --> 19:18.650
He merely asked me if he could 
restore telepathy in the city.

19:18.650 --> 19:19.470
What?

19:19.470 --> 19:21.380
Is there a problem with that?

19:21.380 --> 19:23.640
You'll get to see some 
pretty fireworks soon.

19:23.640 --> 19:25.590
I see. Now, huh?

19:26.520 --> 19:29.590
You're hiding something, aren't you?

19:29.590 --> 19:32.410
You'll see once the telepathy is restored.

19:32.410 --> 19:33.700
But you know, Tomoe...

19:34.350 --> 19:38.170
Maybe destiny is real.

19:38.170 --> 19:40.780
How truly strange.

19:42.270 --> 19:44.350
It's the young master.

19:49.950 --> 19:51.610
What's this?

19:51.940 --> 19:53.350
A single shot.

19:53.350 --> 19:56.390
He masters every skill he learns.

19:56.390 --> 19:59.540
Did he just take out the devices 
planted by the demons?

19:59.990 --> 20:05.310
There are ways to restore telepathic 
communication without destroying it.

20:05.310 --> 20:10.650
Good grief. The demons spent 
months preparing those devices.

20:12.520 --> 20:15.070
Well, good for them.

20:22.500 --> 20:25.730
A state of emergency was declared 
when telepathy was restored?

20:25.730 --> 20:26.860
What's going on?

20:27.280 --> 20:28.730
We're under attack.

20:28.730 --> 20:30.060
Under attack?

20:30.060 --> 20:32.090
By demons, Sairitsu-dono.

20:32.420 --> 20:36.600
We believe demons were responsible 
for this incident, yes, but...

20:36.600 --> 20:38.910
No, the royal capital.

20:38.910 --> 20:39.970
And the imperial capital.

20:41.020 --> 20:46.590
Our nation's hero and the 
priestess of Laurel accompanying her

20:46.590 --> 20:48.470
are probably fighting them.

20:48.470 --> 20:50.430
E-Even Chiya-sama?

20:50.820 --> 20:53.280
Your Majesty, what is the meaning of this?

20:53.280 --> 20:55.940
It doesn't make sense for the 
royal capital to be under attack.

20:55.940 --> 20:57.770
What is the royal army—

20:57.770 --> 20:58.760
Silence!

20:59.790 --> 21:01.520
We don't know the specifics.

21:01.520 --> 21:05.410
But the reality is that demons are 
marching on the imperial capital.

21:05.760 --> 21:08.790
They appeared from 
several directions at once.

21:08.790 --> 21:11.690
In our nation, they appeared by Star Lake.

21:12.130 --> 21:14.800
That puts them just outside 
the royal capital.

21:14.800 --> 21:18.320
Just how many secret plans do they have?

21:18.320 --> 21:19.730
C-Could it be...

21:20.360 --> 21:22.900
Was the disturbance in Rotsgard a decoy?

21:22.900 --> 21:24.350
Probably.

21:24.880 --> 21:29.220
It's probably a coincidence so many 
guests gathered here this year.

21:30.380 --> 21:33.730
But if telepathy was 
restored with this timing,

21:33.730 --> 21:36.740
then it's unlikely Kuzunoha 
is a spy for the demons.

21:36.740 --> 21:38.940
I'm relieved to learn that, as well.

21:38.940 --> 21:44.430
Given the circumstances, we must have 
Kuzunoha teleport us to our nations.

21:52.710 --> 21:55.110
Kuzunoha, we must speak with you.

21:55.880 --> 21:58.090
It's very important.

23:35.000 --> 23:39.510
Night Twenty: 
"The Utterly Hateable Good-For-Nothing."

23:35.220 --> 23:40.020
<b>Next Time</b>

23:36.810 --> 23:40.020
<b>The Utterly Hateable Good-For-Nothing</b>
